🗂️ Data schema

This project works with image files organised into directories, not a single row-and-column CSV table. The notebook references two image collections: a dog-breed image dataset for image-loading and pre-trained-model examples, and a rural/urban image collection for transfer learning.

Expected directory layout

dog-breed-identification/
├── train/
│   └── <image_id>.jpg
└── test/
    └── <image_id>.jpg

rural_and_urban_photos/
├── train/
│   ├── <class_name_1>/
│   │   └── <image_file>.jpg
│   └── <class_name_2>/
│       └── <image_file>.jpg
└── val/
    ├── <class_name_1>/
    │   └── <image_file>.jpg
    └── <class_name_2>/
        └── <image_file>.jpg


The folders above describe the paths expected by the notebook; the datasets are not included with the notebook. The exact rural/urban class-folder names and image counts are not specified in the notebook.

🧾 Image-level schema
Property	Description
Record	One image file
File reference	File path used by the image loader
Image format	The examples use .jpg images
Input size	Images are resized to 224 × 224 pixels
Channels	RGB image channels are loaded into numeric arrays
Preprocessing	ResNet50 preprocess_input function
Label source	Class label inferred from the image's subdirectory by flow_from_directory()
Target classes	Two classes for the rural/urban transfer-learning example
Label encoding	class_mode='categorical'
Classifier output	Two softmax scores, one per configured class
ImageNet inference output	Top-three predicted ImageNet labels for each example image

To confirm the actual mapping between folder names and numeric labels, inspect train_generator.class_indices and validation_generator.class_indices. Ensure the training and validation directories use the same class names and mapping.

